Revision history for Perl extension Sereal-Splitter

0.900_001
  * reject UNDEF_DEADLY (EXTEND 0xff) rather than emitting it in a chunk
  * Upgrade Sereal::Decoder FIRST: chunks of a protocol v5 or v6 input are
    now protocol v5 or v6 documents. Chunks carry the protocol version of
    their input (at least 3, or 4 with zstd) instead of always claiming v3,
    which produced undecodable chunks from v6 input
  * read v5 and v6 input: YES/NO booleans, FLOAT_128, zstd compression and
    keyed checksums (checksum_policy, checksum_vN_key options)
  * compress => SRL_SNAPPY and SRL_ZSTD, and a compress_level option
  * bounds-check all input; reject truncated documents
  * new max_recursion_depth option (default 10000) stops REFP/COPY loops
  * fix a PAD before a value taking that value's place
  * splitters no longer share their lookup tables
  * create_header_data_template() takes an optional protocol version
  * reject a COPY of anything but a string, an OBJECTV whose class name
    is not a string, and a REFP or ALIAS to an untracked item, like
    Sereal::Decoder: expanding them could take exponential time and space
  * built on the reader, buffer and compression code shared with
    Sereal::Encoder and Sereal::Decoder; uthash is no longer bundled

0.840
  * additional fixes for bad crafting of COPY and OBJECTs tags

0.830
  * fix bad crafting of COPY and REFP tags without high bit set while the
    original tag had it

0.820
  * fix memleak

0.810
  * first release considered stable
